    "done_when": "For each of the sixteen shots in imas_ambix/spine_bench/shots.py JT60SA_FROZEN_SHOTSET, imas_ambix/data/selene_psrc.py read_psrc_record(shot, extractor=RemoteEddbExtractor()) runs once, with the default cache root /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa and the default ssh command. Shots go one after another, so one ssh session runs at a time. This fetches only what is uncached, surfABVxp and its time base, into the cache. JT-60SA rules: read-only, one connection at a time, nothing run on the server beyond the extractor's read, no retry loop, no port scan, and nothing read from any home directory. A shot whose fetch fails is recorded with the extractor's own error text, and the next shot is not attempted after a connection-level failure such as a refused or timed-out ssh. Then report blocked with that text, because the lead's tunnel is down. No source file changes. The landing fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-psrc-boundary-fetch.html tabulates, per shot, whether surfABVxp is now cached, its slice count, the valid-vertex range over its slices, and its time span, read back through read_psrc_record from the cache without the extractor. Run on the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set) in the foreground, capturing once to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the head revision and the command and whose last line is EXIT=.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Fill the EDDB cache with PSRC's boundary for the sixteen frozen JT-60SA shots, read-only",
